# Projection model names

When writing or running `run_model`, `backtest`, `report --model`, `dashboard --model`, or `decision_regret --model`:

- Use the exact `BaseModel.name` string from [docs/model_name.md](docs/model_name.md) when specifying a model.
- Champion is `config/model_selection.json` `champion`, not a hardcoded default.
- `commands.run_model`, `commands.report`, `commands.decision_regret`, and `commands.solve` default to Champion when the model is omitted, or when passing `--champion` or `"champion"`.
- `commands.solve` defaults to Champion and ignores stale `data/user_settings.json` `datasource`. `--model` is an explicit CSV override; `--no_hit` restricts solver to 0 hits.
- `commands.backtest` requires an explicit, registered `BaseModel.name`.
- Filename is not the identifier: `models/participation_state_hybrid.py` → `participation_state_hybrid`.
- Unknown / retired Primary names are not aliases: dashboard Refresh falls back to Champion.
- New model: unique `name` property + a catalog row in `docs/model_name.md`.

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — Champion by default
uv run python -m commands.run_model --horizon 5

# ✅ GOOD — Explicit model name from catalog
uv run python -m commands.run_model calibrated_matchup_hybrid --horizon 5

# ✅ GOOD — Explicit backtest of a model
uv run python -m commands.backtest metrics_component_hybrid --gw_range 20-30 --seed_season 2025-26
```
